.TH UNIM-CLI 1 "August 2026" "UNIM 0.4.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
unim\-cli \- Korean/English keyboard converter and UNIM settings manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B unim\-cli
.RI [ OPTIONS ]
.RI [ FILE ...]
.br
.B unim\-cli config
.RI [ SUBCOMMAND ]
.RI [ ARGS ...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B unim\-cli
is a unified command-line tool that offers two modes of operation:
.IP \(bu 2
\fBText conversion\fR (default, when no subcommand is supplied):
an offline batch utility that converts between English keyboard
character streams and composed Hangul. It is independent of the running
.B unim\-daemon
\(em it processes its input as a pure layout transformation.
.IP \(bu 2
\fBSettings management\fR (via the \fBconfig\fR subcommand): reads and
writes the UNIM user configuration file
.RB ( ~/.config/unim/config.yaml ),
using the same configuration backend as the
.B unim\-gui\-gtk
settings dialog and the daemon itself. This is the recommended way to
script configuration changes from shell environments. Changes take
effect immediately for the running daemon via the
.B ConfigChanged
D-Bus signal; no restart is required.
.PP
With no input file in conversion mode, it reads from standard input. With
one or more
.I FILE
arguments, files are processed in order and concatenated to standard
output (or the file given via
.BR \-o ).
.SH CONVERSION OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-compose
Compose an English keyboard stream into Hangul (default mode).
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-decompose
Decompose Hangul into the equivalent English keyboard stream.
.TP
.BR \-o ", " "\-\-output \fIFILE\fR"
Write output to
.IR FILE
instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-k ", " "\-\-korean\-keyboard \fILAYOUT\fR"
Korean keyboard layout. One of
.BR 2bul ", " 390 ", " 391 ", " noshift "."
Default:
.BR 2bul "."
.TP
.BR \-e ", " "\-\-english\-keyboard \fILAYOUT\fR"
English keyboard layout. One of
.BR qwerty ", " dvorak ", " colemak ", " colemak_dh ", " workman "."
Default:
.BR qwerty "."
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print help and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version and exit.
.SH CONFIG SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
.B config show
Print the current configuration summary to standard output.
.TP
.BR "config set" " \fIKEY\fR \fIVALUE\fR"
Set a single configuration key. Run
.B unim\-cli config set \-\-help
for the full list of supported keys (for example
.BR korean\-layout ", " english\-layout ", " default\-category ", "
.BR toggle\-keys ", " auto\-typefix ", "
and the
.B auto\-typefix\-*
family).
.TP
.B config path
Print the absolute path of the active configuration file.
.TP
.B config reset
Reset the configuration file to default values.
.TP
.B config interactive
Launch an interactive prompt-driven configuration session. Useful when a
graphical settings dialog is not available.
.SH EXAMPLES
.PP
Convert a stream of QWERTY keystrokes to Hangul:
.PP
.RS
.nf
echo "dkssudgktpdy" | unim\-cli \-c
.fi
.RE
.PP
Decompose a Hangul file into Dvorak keystrokes:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unim\-cli \-d \-e dvorak input.txt \-o keystrokes.txt
.fi
.RE
.PP
Show current settings and change the Korean layout:
.PP
.RS
.nf
unim\-cli config show
unim\-cli config set korean\-layout 3bul390
.fi
.RE
.SH FILES
.TP
.B ~/.config/unim/config.yaml
The configuration file managed by the \fBconfig\fR subcommand.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR unim (1),
.BR unim\-gui\-gtk (1)
